.TH RANK 1 "July 2026" "rank 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rank \- sort lines of text files, byte-compatible with GNU sort
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rank
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR]...
.br
.B rank
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fB\-\-files0\-from\fR=\fIF\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rank
sorts the concatenation of the given FILEs (or standard input) to
standard output. It is a from-scratch reimplementation of GNU
.BR sort (1)
targeting byte-identical output, diagnostics, and exit codes, with an
MSD byte-radix engine and per-line precomputed key metadata instead of
repeated comparator work.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \fB\-\fR, standard input is read.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Ordering options
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-ignore\-leading\-blanks
Ignore leading blanks when locating sort keys, or, with no keys, skip
leading blanks in the comparison.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dictionary\-order
Consider only blanks and alphanumeric characters.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-ignore\-case
Fold lower case to upper case for comparison.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-general\-numeric\-sort
Compare according to general numerical value (strtold semantics,
including infinities and NaNs).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-human\-numeric\-sort
Compare human-readable numbers (e.g. 2K, 1G).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-nonprinting
Consider only printable characters.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-month\-sort
Compare month names: unknown < JAN < ... < DEC.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-numeric\-sort
Compare according to string numerical value.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-random\-sort
Shuffle by a keyed hash, grouping identical keys. Byte-compatible with
GNU sort's MD5 ordering; with the same \fB\-\-random\-source\fR both
produce the same output.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version\-sort
Natural sort of version numbers within text.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reverse
Reverse the result of comparisons.
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR=\fIWORD\fR
Select the ordering: general\-numeric (g), human\-numeric (h), month
(M), numeric (n), random (R), version (V).
.TP
\fB\-\-random\-source\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Get the 16 random seed bytes from FILE. Fewer than 16 bytes is an
error; extra bytes are ignored.
.PP
Combining ordering modes (for example \fB\-n \-V\fR) is rejected, as in
GNU sort. Global ordering options apply to a key only when that key has
no options of its own.
.SS Key and field options
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR=\fIKEYDEF\fR
Sort by a key. KEYDEF is \fIF\fR[.\fIC\fR][\fIOPTS\fR][,\fIF\fR[.\fIC\fR][\fIOPTS\fR]]
with 1-based field and character positions. OPTS are one or more of
\fBbdfghinrMRV\fR, applying that option to this key only. Obsolete
\fB+POS \-POS\fR syntax is also accepted.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-field\-separator\fR=\fISEP\fR
Use SEP as the field separator; adjacent separators delimit empty
fields. Without \fB\-t\fR, fields are runs of non-blank characters
separated by blanks, and leading blanks belong to the following field.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Annotate the part of each line used for sorting and warn about
questionable key usage.
.SS Other options
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check ", " \-\-check=diagnose\-first
Check whether input is sorted; report the first disorder. Exit status 1
on disorder.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-check=quiet ", " \-\-check=silent
Like \fB\-c\fR without the disorder diagnostic.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-merge
Merge already sorted files; do not sort.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Write to FILE instead of standard output. Sorting a file onto itself is
safe.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stable
Stabilize by disabling the last-resort whole-line comparison.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unique
Output only the first of runs comparing equal under the active keys.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zero\-terminated
Line delimiter is NUL, not newline.
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-buffer\-size\fR=\fISIZE\fR
Use SIZE (with optional K/M/G suffix) for the main memory buffer;
larger inputs sort externally through temporary files.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-temporary\-directory\fR=\fIDIR\fR
Store temporaries in DIR; may be repeated to rotate directories.
.TP
\fB\-\-batch\-size\fR=\fINMERGE\fR
Merge at most NMERGE inputs at once.
.TP
\fB\-\-compress\-program\fR=\fIPROG\fR
Filter temporary files through PROG; PROG must compress standard input
to standard output and decompress with PROG \-d.
.TP
\fB\-\-parallel\fR=\fIN\fR
Use up to N worker threads for large in-memory sorts. Output is
byte-identical to a single-threaded run.
.TP
\fB\-\-files0\-from\fR=\fIF\fR
Read NUL-terminated input file names from F (or standard input when F
is \fB\-\fR); cannot be combined with file operands.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Output version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR LC_COLLATE ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LC_NUMERIC ", " LC_TIME
Honored as in GNU sort. In C/POSIX and probed identity locales rank
sorts raw bytes with its radix engine; other locales use collation
transforms or comparator fallback.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Default location for temporary files when \fB\-T\fR is not given.
.PP
Debug variables, subject to change: \fBRANK_DEBUG_PLAN\fR (print the
selected execution plan), \fBRANK_DEBUG_STATS\fR (engine counters),
\fBRANK_DEBUG_VERIFY\fR (verify output against the scalar comparator),
\fBRANK_FORCE_SCALAR\fR, \fBRANK_FORCE_READ\fR, \fBRANK_PARALLEL_MIN\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when \fB\-c\fR/\fB\-C\fR finds disorder, 2 on error.
.SH NOTES
rank accepts the obsolete \fB+POS \-POS\fR key syntax unconditionally,
where GNU sort requires _POSIX2_VERSION=199209. With \fB\-R\fR combined
with \fB\-d\fR/\fB\-f\fR/\fB\-i\fR in a non-C multibyte locale, rank
hashes ASCII-translated bytes where GNU consults locale tables.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sort (1)
.PP
Full documentation of the parity contract and benchmarks ships in the
source tree.
